# MadGraph5 batch script: p3 r3 > p3 r3 NP<=2
# in vibegraph_toy_color_UFO, restricted by restrict_eps.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The baryonic colour atom Epsilon(1,2,3), which this crate's colour grammar
#   refuses outright. It enters through an s-channel triplet diquark whose two
#   vertices contribute Epsilon and EpsilonBar, so the row measures their
#   contraction rule rather than either atom alone, and the singlet-scalar
#   exchange it interferes with contributes the plain delta-delta structure the
#   contraction has to reduce to.
#
#   Every field of this model is a scalar. Two colour triplets can only be joined
#   into a diquark by a fermion-number-violating vertex if they are fermions, and
#   that needs charge conjugation -- a separate piece of machinery. Scalars keep
#   the row a colour measurement and nothing else.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit because the model declares no coupling at all under
# the QCD order MadGraph's WEIGHTED search reads by name.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_color_UFO-eps
display interactions
generate p3 r3 > p3 r3 NP<=2
output p3r3_to_p3r3_toy_epsilon -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
